// ============================================================================
// RAGNAR.UNK - 2026-07-19 cosmetic dialogue spelling sweep (lv-patched tier)
//
// "Gunnar's's clan" (x2, barks at ~line 543 and ~585) and "Gunnar's clan"
// (x1, bark at ~line 607) -> "Gunnars clan". The clan's name is "Gunnars",
// not "Gunnar": the ten other English references in this file all read
// "the Gunnars" (~lines 890-924) and every German counterpart line reads
// "Gunnars Clan" (~546, ~590, ~610). The 1994 text carried a stray
// possessive, doubled at two of the three sites. All three are inside
// bark() text, not askList or case matcher strings, so no menu dispatch is
// affected. No other byte of the file is changed.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// RAGNAR.UNK - Lost Vale restoration patched copy (lv-patched tier)
//
// Byte-copy of "shared/data/lv-usecode/UNK files/UNK/RAGNAR.UNK" (the
// recovered 1994 snapshot) plus the minimal fixes below, all from the
// 2026-07-04 quest-path survey (quest step-7 repair). Line numbers
// refer to the ORIGINAL unpatched file; this header shifts everything
// below it.
//
// 1. line 118: was `ragnarMet = false;` -> now commented out
//    (1994 debug leftover: use() reset the met flag on every
//    conversation, so the met-branch menu could never be reached).
// 2. line 386: was `There is goodeness in all.` -> now
//    `There is goodness in all.` (menu add must match its case at
//    line 394; kept the correct spelling).
// 3. line 424: was `You are a cautious fellow` -> now
//    `You are a cautious fellow.` (menu add must match its case at
//    line 432 and its removal at line 456, both with the period).
// 4. lines 522/532/538: was `Yes, I do.` -> now `Yes, I do like her.`
//    (Thordis-crush pair renamed, menu add AND case AND removal: the
//    case at 532 shadowed the Passage-Stone `Yes, I do.` case at 760,
//    so the stone/legends/bag subtree could never dispatch).
// 5. line 701: was `He spoke of you and his daughter.` -> now
//    `He spoke of you and Hrodny.` (menu add must match its case at
//    line 860 and its removal at line 878; Ragnar's reply echoes the
//    name as if the player said it).
// 6. line 724: was `How do know so much?` -> now
//    `How do you know so much?` (menu add must match its case at
//    line 731 and its removal at line 740).
// 7. line 920: was `Do you know of the speaking stone?` -> now
//    `Do you know of the Passage Stone?` (menu add must match its
//    case at line 745; Passage Stone is the wording used everywhere
//    else in the final dialogue).
// 8. after line 372: RESTORATION ADDITION (no 1994 counterpart) -
//    was: no case handler for `I have no fight with you.` (the menu
//    add at line 355 dead-ended; picking it silently looped) -> now:
//    a minimal case that barks one in-character line, removes its own
//    ask, and continues the menu loop. No exit, no flags.
//
// ---- 2026-07-05 playtest reachability repair (steps 5-12 punch list) ----
// The 2026-07-05 in-engine playtest found the whole tale-and-bag beat
// dead in natural play and three cosmetic/dispatch defects. Fixes:
//
// 9. line 183 (met-branch top menu): was `if sentToRagnar` gating the
//    `Atli sent me to you.` add -> now `if (atliMet = true) and
//    (ragnarToldStone = false)`, and the add itself was `askList^=`
//    -> now `askList+=`. sentToRagnar (bit 0x449) is a DECLARED flag
//    that NOTHING in the entire build ever writes (verified: no
//    `pop global 0449h`), so all three `Atli sent me to you.` add
//    sites were permanently dead and the entire subtree hanging off it
//    (Atli admires you -> ... -> Do you know of the Passage Stone? ->
//    Yes, I do. -> Why do you not go there?, which sets ragnarToldStone
//    and spawns the lake-ruins bag) was unreachable. The two other add
//    sites do not help in natural play: the "You are a cautious fellow."
//    site (line ~508) offers the blame line, not the referral, once
//    atliMet is set (which it always is by step 7), and the "I wish to
//    apologize." site needs the ragnarPissed path. The top-menu site is
//    the faithful entry (Atli sent you -> mention it when you return to
//    Ragnar), so it is re-gated on atliMet (the durable "you have met
//    Atli" flag, bit 0x457, the natural proxy for "Atli referred you").
//    `not ragnarToldStone` stops the referral (and thus a second bag
//    spawn at the fixed lake-ruins point 16447,25727,64) from re-
//    appearing once Ragnar has already told the tale. `^=` -> `+=`
//    because a union onto the still-empty met-branch askList is dropped
//    by the engine (the D11 note); append is not. Writing sentToRagnar
//    on Atli's side was the alternative but is strictly larger (an ATLI
//    patch PLUS this same `^=`->`+=` fix) and no more faithful, so the
//    single-file re-gate was chosen.
// 10. lines 171/177: the two opening greeting barks were SWAPPED - the
//    met branch barked "Greetings I say." and the UNMET (first-meeting)
//    branch barked "So we meet again.". Swapped the English so the
//    unmet branch shows the fresh greeting and the met branch the
//    reunion line. Only the English sentences were exchanged; the \g
//    German halves (stripped from the build) were left in place.
// 11. line 373: was `g\ Ja, ich habe Thordis getroffen.` (transposed
//    marker) -> now `\g Ja, ...`. The lexer only strips from `\f`/`\g`;
//    `g\` was not recognized, so the German leaked into the
//    `Yes, I have met Thordis.` menu OPTION string, which then no longer
//    matched its case label (line ~644, correct `\g`) - a dead pick, not
//    just a cosmetic leak. The `\g` now strips it to English.
// 12. line 242 ("When you can find game?" case): was a redundant
//    `askList+=<<"When you can find game?">>;` that re-added the very
//    option being handled -> now `askList-=` (consume it, matching every
//    sibling case's self-removal). Removes the duplicate menu entry.
//
// Known 1994 quirks deliberately NOT fixed (outside the minimal
// mandate; recorded in the step-7 survey report): none left. The
// crush/stone `No, I don't.` collision this paragraph listed until
// 2026-10-10 is fixed by change 15, and the three menu-string quirks it
// also listed are fixed by change 14 below.
//
// ---- 2026-10-08 schedule destinations (Douglas's decision) ----
// 13. lines 43-45 and 60-62 (2026-10-08, Douglas's decision): the
//    schedule() destinations retargeted to the rebuilt Map 10. Both
//    1994 points were pre-rebuild coordinates at z 64 over z-0 ground
//    (docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave1.md). Slot timing is unchanged;
//    only the x/y/z literals move. Home (eventide): (14207,13055,64) ->
//    (5439,10527,0), south of the Hoskuld edge hut (hut lot 5). In the
//    field (every other period; he is a hunter): (13695,19071,64) ->
//    (7039,17151,0), the west clearing south of Hoskuld. METHOD
//    safeTeleport/canSafeTeleport are called for real from the same day
//    (u8c_symbols.METHOD_ROUTINES): retail teleports exactly to the
//    point, checking only that the Avatar is over 700 units from both
//    the NPC and the point, so
//    agents/map-populator/src/test_schedule_destinations.py checks
//    every compiled destination with exact_reach on the built
//    FIXED.DAT.
//
// ---- 2026-10-10 menu near-misses ----
// 14. lines 357, 706 and 794 (2026-10-10): the three menu strings the
//    step-7 survey left, now that test_uc_dialogue.py D19b's near-miss
//    scan pins every such string and D19c walks the reachable ones. Each
//    is changed on the side its two siblings disagree with:
//    - line 357, the removal in case "Yes, I'm peaceful." (line 342):
//      `Yes, I am peaceful.` -> `Yes, I'm peaceful.`, the add's (332)
//      and the case's text (two bytes shorter). The case goes on
//      talking, so the answered option stayed on the first-meeting menu.
//    - line 706, the removal in case "I believe that he is sincere."
//      (693): `I believe that is sincere.` -> `... that he is ...`, the
//      add's (669) text (three bytes longer); same effect.
//    - line 794: the add `Her body was eaten?!` -> `?`, the text of its
//      case (798) and removal (802) (one byte shorter), so the pick
//      dispatches. Reached on the stone thread ("Do you know of the
//      Passage Stone?" -> "Yes, I do." -> "Tell me of the legends." ->
//      "How was she killed?"), which change 9 made reachable.
//
// ---- 2026-10-10 exhaustive menu scan (D19b) ----
// 15. lines 183, 756, 769 and 852 (2026-10-10): the two reachable defects
//    the exhaustive scan (every removal never added, every add never
//    answered, every case shadowed) found here:
//    - line 183, the removal in case "What do you do here?" (line 178):
//      `What do you do?` -> `What do you do here?`, the text of the add
//      (163) and the case, so the answered option leaves the
//      first-meeting menu (docs/playtest-2026-10-10-dialogue.md finding
//      1: it never did).
//    - lines 756, 769 and 852: the Passage-Stone answer `No, I don't.`
//      -> `No, I don't` (no period), the text of its own 1994 case at
//      line 841 ("Then why bother me..."), in the add (756) and both
//      removals (769, 852). With the period the pick matched the
//      crush/Thordis case "No, I don't.", "No, I haven't." (542) first,
//      which barks "Blind are you? Stupid? Wonderful she is..." and
//      ends the conversation. Same collision class as change 4, fixed on
//      the stone side because that side's 1994 case already differs.
//      The German halves are untouched.
//
// ---- 2026-10-10 replies written for the restoration (Douglas's decision) ----
// 16. after lines 514, 881 and 924 (2026-10-10; LV restoration text, not
//    1994): cases for the three options test_uc_dialogue.py D19b found
//    with no reply anywhere. Each is a short bark in his voice built only
//    from facts already in this file, with a German half in the file's
//    style, and removes the answered option:
//    a. "Who is Thordis?" (add, line 507, in case "What have they done?"
//       when thordisMet is unset, just after "tell you Thordis will"):
//       his own words for her ("A great woman Thordis is! Not only a
//       shrewd leader she is ...", 603), and go and ask her.
//    b. "Do you like her?" (873, Hrodny, after "No Thordis she is, but
//       beautiful still.", 865): the same, gruffer.
//    c. "None, thank you." (909, after "Help you already I have. Told
//       you where I think the speaking stone lies", 902): go and find it,
//       and beware the undead water creatures that ran him off the ruins
//       (822-827).
//    Every new line is marked `// LV restoration text 2026-10-10 (not
//    1994)`.
// 17. after line 597 (2026-10-11): case "Yes, I have met Thordis.", "I
//    met someone named Thordis." (582) removed only its first label, so the
//    greeting's "I met someone named Thordis." (148, thordisMet without
//    spokeOfThordis) stayed on the menu, and a second pick appended "Thordis
//    is a good person." / "I was not impressed." again. One added removal
//    of it. Found by test_uc_dialogue.py D19b's sibling class.
// ============================================================================

uses "npc";                                                                                                                      
uses "flags";
uses "item";
uses "free";
uses "snddefs";

npcclass Ragnar inherits Npc
{
	process look();
	process use();
	process schedule (currentTime:Long);
	process enterFastArea();
	process leaveFastArea();
	process cast(ref:Referent);
}

process Ragnar::look()
{
	if ragnarName
	{
		bark ("Ragnar
		\g Ragnar");
	}
	else
	{
		bark ("Man
		\g Mann");
	}
}

process Ragnar::schedule(currentTime:Long)
{

	point : WorldPoint;
	map : MapNum = 10;


	//home

   if (getPeriod() = eventide)
	
	{
		point.x = 5439;
		point.y = 10527;
		point.z =0;
	}



	//in the field


	if (getPeriod() = firstebb) 
	or (getPeriod() = lastebb)
	or (getPeriod()=bloodwatch) 
	or (getPeriod() = daytide)
	or (getPeriod()= threemoons)

	{
		point.x = 7039;
		point.y = 17151;
		point.z = 0;
	}


	safeTeleport(point,map);
}

process Ragnar::enterFastArea()
{
	if isDead()
	{
		return;
	}

	cSetActivity(ACT_LOITER);
}


process Ragnar::leaveFastArea()
{
	killProcess(referent,PT_ACTIVITY);
}


process Ragnar::cast(ref:Referent)
{
	count:Number;
	count = 10;
	while (not getTarget()) and (count)
	{
		wait(1);
		count--;
	}

	ref=getTarget();
	if ref = Avatar:Referent
	{
		spawn callTheShades() -> return;

		if not isDead()
		{
			killProcess(referent,PT_ACTIVITY);
			killProcess(referent,PT_BARK);
			bark("Help! Help!
				\g Hilfe! Hilfe!");
		}
	}
}


process Ragnar::use()
{
	enterConvo();   

	answer:String = "";
	askList: String List;
//	ragnarMet = false;		// LV-RESTORE change 1: 1994 debug reset removed

	if ragnarMet
	{
		bark ("So we meet again.
			\g Sei gegrÅ·t.");
	}
	else
	{
// @@@ CHANGE F G
		bark ("Greetings I say.
		\g Sei gegrÅ·t, Avatar.");
	}

	if ragnarMet
	{
 		if (atliMet = true) and (ragnarToldStone = false)
		{
		 	askList+=<<"Atli sent me to you.
							\g Atli hat mich zu dir geschickt."	>>;
		}
		
		if thordisMet
		{
			if spokeOfThordis
			{
				askList+=<<"I have met Thordis.">>;
			}
			else
			{
				askList+=<<"I met someone named Thordis.">>;
			}
		}
		
		if ragnarPissed
		{
			askList=<<"Ragnar?">>;
		}
			   
  		
	}
	else
	{
		askList = <<"What is your name?
			\g Wie hei·t du?", 
			"What do you do here?
			\g Was machst du hier?">>;
		ragnarMet = true;
	}
 while answer != "Farewell."
	{
		askList -= <<"Farewell.
				\g Lebwohl.">>;
		askList += <<"Farewell.
				\g Lebwohl.">>;
		answer = ask(askList);
		switch answer
		{

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "What do you do here?"
			{
				bark("Do here? Hard to understand you are. Strangly you
				speak. But try to answer your question I will. A hunter I am.
				Bring back food for the clan I do. When find it I can.");
				askList-=<<"What do you do here?">>;
				askList+=<<"When you can find game?">>;
			}

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "When you can find game?"
			{
				bark("Not easy it is. Dry this land is...and barren. Little
				game to hunt there is. Wild torax, mainly. Remember stories
				I do about the old days.");
				askList-=<<"When you can find game?">>;
				askList+=<<"The old days?">>;

			}

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "The old days?"
			{
				bark("Stories my grandmother told. Plenty of game
				these was, she said. Walk out the door of your
				house you could and waiting	the game would be.
				Plentiful and big. Feed an entire village just one
				could.");
				askList-=<<"The old days?">>;
				askList+=<<"What kind of game?", "What happened to them?">>;
			
			}


// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "What kind of game?"
			{
				bark("Bigger than a torax they were. Out of their head two
				horns grew. Spread as wide as your arms, the horns did. Tined
				the horns were, and as sharp as knives. Kill you as quick
				as look at you, they would. Covered with a short fine hair
				their bodies were. Used to make clothes their skins were.
				Then other game there was. Some big, some small. Small
				creatures that flew in the sky there were and large
				creatures that fed on grasses. Wish I could see them, I do.");
				askList-=<<"What kind of game?">>;
			}

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "What happened to them?"
			{
				bark("History don't you know? The same thing that happend
				to our land it was. The Great Cataclysm. Dried up the water,
				it did. All but the hardiest plants it killed. So died
				off the game did. Now, barely survive the few wild torax
				do.");
				askList-=<<"What happened to them?">>;
			}
			
			
// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "Ragnar?"
			{
				bark("Told you I did wish to see you I do not. Why back
				bothering me are you?");
				askList-=<<"Ragnar?">>;
				askList+=<<"Nothing.", "I wish to apologize.">>;
			}
// @@@ CHANGE F G			
			case "Nothing."
			{
				bark("Then out of my sight get!");
				exitConvo();
				return;
			}

// @@@ CHANGE F G			
			case "I wish to apologize."
			{
				bark("Well, not a vengful man I am. Forgiven all is. Now,
				What do for you can I?");
// LV-RESTORE change 12: clear ragnarPissed here. The bark says "Forgiven
// all is" but the flag stayed set, and the top menu at the head of use()
// does `askList=<<"Ragnar?">>` -- an ASSIGNMENT, not an append -- so every
// later conversation collapsed to that one option again. Apologising
// restored the menu for the rest of that one conversation and nothing
// more. Anger him once and the Passage Stone thread, and with it the bag
// that quest step 7 hands over, was unreachable for the rest of the game.
				ragnarPissed = false;
				askList-=<<"I wish to apologize.", "Nothing.">>;
				if (sentToRagnar = true) and (hasMark = false)
				{
					askList^=<<"Atli sent me to you.
								\g Atli hat mich zu dir geschickt.">>;
				}
				
				if (thordisMet = true)
				{
					askList^=<<"I have met Thordis.">>;
				}
				askList^=<<"Tell me of the Vale.">>;
			} 												

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "Tell me of the Vale."
			{
				bark("What to tell there is? A barren, dry place it is.
				Little game to hunt there is. Wander far and wide I must
				fresh meat to find. Mostly torax I hunt. Caught one of
				those flying evil thing once I did. Not too good for eating
				they are. Greasy.");
				askList-=<<"Tell me of the Vale.">>;
			}


// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "What is your name?
				\g Wie hei·t du?"
			{
				bark ("Ragnar called I am. Never seen one such as you
					have I. Where come from do you?
					\g Ragnar hei·e ich. Wahrlich, so einen wie dich
					hab' ich noch nie gesehen. Woher kommst du?");
				askList += <<"From very far away.
						\g Von sehr weit her.", 

						"I am new to your land.
						\g Ich bin neu in deinem Land.">>;
				askList -= <<"What is your name?
						\g Wie hei·t du?">>;
				ragnarName = true;
			}

// @@@ CHANGE F G
			case "I am new to your land.
						\g Ich bin neu in deinem Land."
				{
				bark("Obvious that is. Know all places in the Vale I do.
				Saying you come from outside the Vale are you? Believe
				it I do not.");
				askList-=<<"I am new to your land.
						\g Ich bin neu in deinem Land.">>;
				}



			case "From very far away.
			\g Von sehr weit her."
				{
					if thordisMet
					{
						bark ("The stranger Thordis talked to you must be.
						\g Du mu·t der Fremde sein, mit dem Thordis gesprochen hat.");
						askList += <<"Yes, I have met Thordis.
								\g Ja, ich habe Thordis getroffen.">>;
					}
					else
					{ 
						bark ("Know that I do! Never seen anything like you I have. 
						Come in peace do you?
							\g FÅrwahr, das wei· ich. Wahrlich, ich habe nie so etwas wie
							dich gesehen. Kommst du in Frieden?");
						askList += <<"Yes, I'm peaceful.
								\g Ja, ich bin friedfertig.", 

								"Leave me alone.
								\g La· mich in Ruhe.">>;
					}
					askList -= <<"From very far away.
							\g Von sehr weit her.">>;
				}
			
			case "Yes, I'm peaceful.
					\g Ja, ich bin friedfertig."

			    {
				bark ("Peacful you are, but peaceful with Gunnar clan? If peaceful
						with Gunnar clan you are, then at war with Huskold clan
						you are.
						\g Friedfertig bist du, aber in Frieden mit dem Gunnar
						Clan? Im Frieden mit dem Gunnar Clan zu sein hei·t im
						Krieg mit dem Huskold Clan zu sein.");
			      
					askList += <<"I am peaceful with all.
						\g Ich lebe mit allen in Frieden.", 
						"I have no fight with you.
						\g Ich habe keinen Streit mit dir.">>;
					askList -= <<"Yes, I'm peaceful.
						\g Ja, ich bin friedfertig.">>;
			    }

			case "Leave me alone.
			\g La· mich in Ruhe."
				{
				bark ("Then do so I will. Rude stranger you are. Go from here now!
					\g Das werde ich tun. Wahrlich, ein unhîflicher Fremder bist
					du. Verschwinde jetzt!");
					askList -= <<"Leave me alone.
					\g La· mich in Ruhe.">>;
				ragnarPissed = true;
					exitConvo();
					return;
				 }
			     
// >>> LV-RESTORE change 8 (restoration addition): the ask above at
// line 355 ("Yes, I'm peaceful." case) had no case handler anywhere
// in the 1994 source, so picking it silently looped back to the
// menu. One in-character bark, remove own ask, continue the loop;
// no exit, no flags.
			case "I have no fight with you.
				\g Ich habe keinen Streit mit dir."
				{
					bark ("Then no quarrel between us there is.");
					askList -= <<"I have no fight with you.
						\g Ich habe keinen Streit mit dir.">>;
				}

		    case "I am peaceful with all.
			\g Ich lebe mit allen in Frieden."
				 {                                                   
					bark ("Then a fool you are. No disrespect do I mean, but
						  be peaceful with all a man cannot be.
						  Too many others there are who would not be 
						  peaceful with you.
							\g Dann bist du ein Narr. Nimm's mir
							nicht Åbel, aber ein Mann kann
			   				nicht mit allen in Frieden leben. Es
							gibt zu viele andere, die nicht
							in Frieden mit dir leben wollen.");
					askList += <<"There is goodness in all.
									\g In allen Menschen steckt etwas Gutes.", 
								"You have a point.
									\g Da hast du recht.">>;
					askList -= <<"I am peaceful with all.
									\g Ich lebe mit allen in Frieden.">>;
				 }
			     
			case "There is goodness in all.
				\g In allen Menschen steckt etwas Gutes."
				 {
					bark ("How naive you are. The body of a grown man you have
						but in it the mind of a child there is. Led such
						a sheltered life you must have. Never have
						had to face adversity, have you?
							\g Wie naiv du bist. Du hast fÅrwahr den Kîrper eines
							erwachsenen Mannes, aber darin steckt der Verstand eines 
							Kindes. Wahrlich, du mu·t ein wohlbehÅtetes Leben gefÅhrt 
							haben. Du hast wohl nie Probleme gehabt.");
					askList -= <<"There is goodness in all.
						\g In allen Menschen steckt etwas Gutes.">>;     
				 }       
								
	    case "You have a point.
		\g Da hast du recht."
			 {
				bark ("Yes, not unwise it is to greet people
					with kindness but be wary
					of them until know them you do. But
					unwise it is to believe that good all people
					are. A great capacity for
					wicked behavior people have.

						\g Ja, es ist sinnvoll, Leute freundlich zu begrÅ·en, aber
						vorsichtig zu sein, bis man sie kennt. Wahrlich, es ist nÑrrisch zu
						glaubem, da· alle Leute gut sind. Menschen kînnen ungemein bîse
						sein.");

					askList += <<"You are a cautious fellow.
						\g Du bist ein vorsichtiger Kerl.", 
						"Yes, people can be wicked.
						\g Ja, Leute kînnen bîse sein.">>;
